[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630693877","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327#issuecomment-2630693877","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102327","id":2630693877,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6czTP1","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T11:34:15Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T11:34:15Z","body":"This is a bit of a complicated edge case of circular references, the Ref is kept alive because it is used and has a circular reference to itself, this is not too different from keeping a reference to self inside as a property, though this is more surprising\n\nI don't think this can be easily solved, especially not without causing bugs elsewhere, the behavior of keeping the item alive is technically correct I'd say, and it'd be hard to detect this case differently from, for example, connecting this same method to some other signal where you *want* the object to survive","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630693877/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630977852","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327#issuecomment-2630977852","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102327","id":2630977852,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6c0Yk8","user":{"login":"call-me-void","id":3617863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MTc4NjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3617863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void","html_url":"https://github.com/call-me-void","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T13:14:55Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T13:15:04Z","body":"I agree that this behavior is technically correct, but it can be confusing — especially when you're not capturing self directly but rather inner variables of the class. Perhaps we could at least issue a runtime warning in debug mode.\n\nRegarding case detection, I believe we could check the signal owner when connecting at runtime. Essentially, if the signal belongs to the same object, the lambda should either capture a weak reference (as a potential fix) or print a warning about a possible circular reference.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630977852/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630982569","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327#issuecomment-2630982569","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102327","id":2630982569,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6c0Zup","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T13:16:43Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T13:16:43Z","body":"But then you just move the limit one step back, what if A is bound to B which is bound to A? Also detecting isn't trivial here, as it would require detecting where something is used\n\nWhat if the callable is created and then used later, or in two signals, etc.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630982569/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2631072256","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327#issuecomment-2631072256","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102327","id":2631072256,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6c0voA","user":{"login":"call-me-void","id":3617863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MTc4NjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3617863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void","html_url":"https://github.com/call-me-void","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/call-me-void/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T13:54:36Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T13:54:36Z","body":"I guess you're right. \n\nPerhaps we should at least provide additional debug information about leaked objects. I've determined that the leaked `GDScriptNativeClass` appears to be an internal GDScript class used for creating engine classes, and it isn't particularly relevant in this situation. However, it would be really useful if the output indicated that the leaked objects are instances of `RefCountedClass` along with their associated script object (I suspect that's what the second leaked object is, though I'm not 100% sure).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2631072256/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4870095235","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327#issuecomment-4870095235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102327","id":4870095235,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIkfBgw","user":{"login":"chaysest","id":78029165,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MDI5MTY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78029165?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest","html_url":"https://github.com/chaysest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chaysest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-02T20:13:03Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T20:13:03Z","body":"I believe this is/is related to an issue I've been experiencing on 4.7.stable\n\nI definitely understand that this behavior is correct/intended to a certain degree. However, there can definitely be some serious and unexpected side-effects of the leaked objects. \n\nFrom my testing it seems that the Ref that is kept alive due to the Lambda will also cause any SubResources / Sub-RefCounted to also leak objects, which sort of makes sense since the original 'parent' object still references them in some way? \n\nThis also doesn't seem to be documented well that I could find and it was starting to have a serious impact on a project of mine. I was creating lots of resources with subresources and couldn't figure out why there were tons of leaked objects happening even after de-referencing the parent resources. (which eventually caused fps/memory usage issues)  \n\nI created a little demo when I was debugging this and figured I'd add it here if it helps with the discussion. If this isn't something that can be reasonable changed in the engine, a warning/error in the editor when using a lambda in this way would be a great place to start IMO. \n\n[memory-leak-demo-v4.7.stable.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29612081/memory-leak-demo-v4.7.stable.zip)\n\nThe demo project also shows how confusing this behavior can be where doing something like this results in the expected behavior:\n\n```gdscript\n\nclass_name Good extends Resource \n\n@export var callable = test_callable\n\nfunc test_callable(): \n   print(\"Hello World\")\n\n```\n\nWhereas this leaks objects with no warning/error, the only way to tell is by watching the Object count go up in the Debug Monitor afaik: \n\n```gdscript\n\nclass_name Bad extends Resource \n\n@export var callable = func(): test_callable()\n\nfunc test_callable(): \n   print(\"Hello World\")\n\n```\n\nObviously the first one is just a cleaner option between the two when looking at it in a vacuum. While debugging my project it was extremely unclear that the lambda was the culprit since it wasn't being called or used in any way while running the project. In my case it was just a tool button.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4870095235/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887174131","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327#issuecomment-4887174131","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102327","id":4887174131,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0xb8w","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T18:40:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T18:40:33Z","body":"Should be fixable by cleaning up references hold by `GDScriptLambdaCallable` (and the self version) when shutting down `GDScriptLanguage`. However we currently don't do bookkeeping about `GDScriptLambdaCallable`, so a closer look at potential performance impacts might be needed.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887174131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5992942328","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327#issuecomment-5992942328","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102327","id":5992942328,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZTUK-A","user":{"login":"40-4","id":92892668,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYlt_A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92892668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4","html_url":"https://github.com/40-4","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/40-4/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T10:48:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T10:55:09Z","body":"Hi, is this issue is being working on? I've recently been tracking memory leaks in my project too and found this issue. I don't quite get when lambda captures the self and when not, so currently i'm in the process of removing almost all lambdas from the codebase.\n\nCould someone please explain to me what usages of self in lambda functions causes leaks? Could using the weakref() every time i need to access self or one of it methods solve the issue?\nThanks in advance","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5992942328/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]